 Linear Transformation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124748 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186125401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124748 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124748 #edb/ref 1050 960.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124748 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "91d90bfa-8f19-5546-aba3-f391b0f30b02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125401 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125401 #edb/ref 1061 20015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125401 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f42af34b-8f66-5aee-9bd5-7a3de03f5cdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125401 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125402 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125402 #edb/ref 1061 20016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125402 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddfd46cc-2853-59ef-ace0-92fabfa7af70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125402 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125403 #edb/ref 1061 20017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125403 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb409d13-a534-5413-97fd-7e71ad7fbfad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125403 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125448 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125448 #edb/ref 1061 20424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125448 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "905da979-387e-5ded-9c78-3ede6dac59ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125448 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125490 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125490 #edb/ref 1061 25971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125490 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb766bed-08ee-564c-a45c-c20f57e59be3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125490 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125497 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125497 #edb/ref 1061 26848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125497 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f45ab6b-4ad9-5e42-8a3f-69ef72e1a03c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125497 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125783 #edb/ref 1064 "The **image** (or **range**) of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is the set of all vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ that the transformation maps to. That is to say\n![](images/4c/4c89132f0fd9713f0e688f7cf00189bf4d3f27baddad032c74edf7b0a8c0d8ee.svg)\n\nThe diagram below gives a schematic representation of the image of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}: V \\rightarrow V$ for a vector space $V.$\n\n![](images/b8/b859250756eb3870f9c1d4d7e6e78f044adf2b0c4cd94a87d01011879d668afc.png)\n\nNotice that $\\mathbf{0}$ is always in the image of a linear transformation since $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nAs an example, let's consider the linear transformation\n![](images/61/618376922e3c837dba3f742fd77340c2a3deee6cee099843232f85bcec5faf93.svg)\n\nNotice that, for example, the vector $\\mathbf b = [6,9]^T$ is in the image of the transformation $\\mathbf{S}$ since there is another vector $\\mathbf{u} = [1,1]^T$ such that $\\mathbf{S}(\\mathbf{u})=\\mathbf{b}{:}$\n\n![](images/51/51004801582ad1a6cddc389e07a4ac8d486c410ebacf264de14ac1a798a10c30.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125783 #edb/ref 1065 3530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125783 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "70bccafd-705b-5026-bdf8-ef7731dfcc77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125783 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125819 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, the image of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is equivalent to the column space of its standard matrix $T.$ That is,\n![](images/6e/6e8b0992ade86b8e8a0c7d2227ff5473f5cae843f8e763e556c17654e7f1f143.svg)\n\nSo to find out if a vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is in the image of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we just need to check if the matrix equation $T\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125819 #edb/ref 1065 4276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125819 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f52415b1-727f-53a7-8502-857fdcb3b835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125819 #edb/ref 1067 "Determining If a Vector Lies in the Image" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125821 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, the rank of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is equal to the dimension of its image:\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(\\mathbf{T}) = \\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(\\mathbf{T}))\n$$\n\nIf the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ has the standard matrix $T,$ then the dimension of the image is equal to the rank of $T{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(\\mathbf{T})) = \\text{rank}(T)\n$$\n\nSo, in general, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(\\mathbf{T}) = \\text{rank}(T).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125821 #edb/ref 1065 4382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125821 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "89b10851-3eed-5f36-a0ab-c9d0610e9b75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125821 #edb/ref 1067 "The Rank of a Linear Transformation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186367436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186368554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175