 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186367429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1039 "Constructing the Normal Equation Corresponding to a Linear System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133822 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fda08f5d-4513-5be0-b8c4-475e82f9bf5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1045 "The Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System (With Collinearity)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186134698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1050 1200.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134027 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dac16d4a-58b8-5e9c-b569-e42a4c036b80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1061 20272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "73e4890e-8287-5a80-8c3c-2c95ce05512e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134698 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1061 20273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2664b077-4f38-5154-af4c-d4fd21596b27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134699 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1061 20275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4594719-c6f8-53f5-bc1a-22e17b863c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134700 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1061 22147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a43860da-1a59-5a1c-930e-23d6f893c13a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134733 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following inconsistent system of equations:\n\n![](images/6b/6bcdc34077d88eac5ed89d408a1d2525b617a4f427b13433757df918585d380f.svg)\n\nSince the system is inconsistent, we cannot find an exact solution. However, as we've previously seen, we can attempt to find the so-called least-squares solution, which is a vector ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\|  A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\|\n$$\n\nis as small as possible. \n\nAs before, the least-squares solution can be found by solving the corresponding normal equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, note the following: \n\n- Previously, we solved the normal equation by left-multiplying the normal equation by $(A^T A)^{-1}.$\n\n- However, in this case, the second column of $A$ is a multiple of the first.\n\n- So, the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent.\n\n- Therefore, $A^T A$ is not invertible.\n\nTo solve the normal equation in this case, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -20 \\\\ -20 & 80\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the last equation by Gaussian elimination, we obtain the general solution\n\n![](images/b9/b93bd5cb988f208eb26115bfaa08e81be989ee79cf3655612c1a0522a5566d95.svg)\n\nNotice that our solution is not unique! The second term of the least-squares solution (highlighted in blue) represents vectors from the null space of $A.$ \n\nIn general, if a matrix $A$ has collinear columns, then the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf x = \\mathbf b$ is not unique." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1065 3637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2f2e227a-264e-5e00-8c12-ea534f4b351f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135060 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186161271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186161272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186161273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186161274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186161275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186161271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161270 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8d12cea6-72a7-5022-a590-7c09e6cf36dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161271 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161271 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161271 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "